{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123627","id":4576507905,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEMf4AQ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123627","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123627.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123627.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123627","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123627/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123627/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123627/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/df66c6982dd01e0af136745a4fc9248796dfa329","number":123627,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Use validated utility calls for implicitly convertible arguments in GDScript","user":{"login":"YYF233333","id":67693830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NjkzODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67693830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333","html_url":"https://github.com/YYF233333","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Related to #85514\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/contribution_rules.html#explain-your-contributions\r\n-->\r\n\r\nUtility function validated calls will do `VariantCaster::cast` internally, so arg types do not need to match the signature exactly to be able to use validated path. This PR relaxes the condition to implicitly convertiable (`Variant::can_convert_strict`), which means calls like `sin(int)` now use the validated path.\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>benchmark</summary>\r\n\r\n`scons production=yes scu_build=yes tests=yes`\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>code</summary>\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nextends Node2D\r\n\r\nconst OUTER_LOOPS = 10\r\nconst INNER_LOOPS = 1000000\r\n\r\nfunc _ready():\r\n\tfor i in OUTER_LOOPS:\r\n\t\tprint(\"\\n%s:\" % i)\r\n\r\n\t\tvar start : int\r\n\t\tvar end : int\r\n\r\n\t\tstart = Time.get_ticks_usec()\r\n\t\tfor j in INNER_LOOPS:\r\n\t\t\tvar ret : float = sin(j)\r\n\t\t\t#assert(ret == sin(float(j)))\r\n\t\tend = Time.get_ticks_usec()\r\n\t\tprint(end - start, \" us\")\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\tstart = Time.get_ticks_usec()\r\n\t\tfor j in INNER_LOOPS:\r\n\t\t\tvar ret : float = sin(float(j))\r\n\t\tend = Time.get_ticks_usec()\r\n\t\tprint(end - start, \" us\")\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\tstart = Time.get_ticks_usec()\r\n\t\tfor j in INNER_LOOPS:\r\n\t\t\tvar ret : Vector2 = Vector2.from_angle(j)\r\n\t\tend = Time.get_ticks_usec()\r\n\t\tprint(end - start, \" us\")\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>result</summary>\r\n\r\nmaster:\r\n```bash\r\n0:\r\n94009 us\r\n105766 us\r\n97823 us\r\n\r\n1:\r\n91278 us\r\n105575 us\r\n98156 us\r\n\r\n2:\r\n90921 us\r\n105686 us\r\n97843 us\r\n\r\n3:\r\n90840 us\r\n105632 us\r\n98137 us\r\n\r\n4:\r\n90905 us\r\n105864 us\r\n98045 us\r\n\r\n5:\r\n91430 us\r\n105796 us\r\n98015 us\r\n\r\n6:\r\n90876 us\r\n105849 us\r\n97942 us\r\n\r\n7:\r\n90863 us\r\n105746 us\r\n98047 us\r\n\r\n8:\r\n91344 us\r\n106600 us\r\n98974 us\r\n\r\n9:\r\n91980 us\r\n106704 us\r\n98935 us\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis PR:\r\n```bash\r\n0:\r\n95386 us\r\n109648 us\r\n98072 us\r\n\r\n1:\r\n89840 us\r\n105614 us\r\n98183 us\r\n\r\n2:\r\n90101 us\r\n105921 us\r\n98100 us\r\n\r\n3:\r\n89842 us\r\n105501 us\r\n97985 us\r\n\r\n4:\r\n89769 us\r\n105561 us\r\n98199 us\r\n\r\n5:\r\n89997 us\r\n105509 us\r\n98116 us\r\n\r\n6:\r\n89928 us\r\n105530 us\r\n98036 us\r\n\r\n7:\r\n89934 us\r\n105448 us\r\n98134 us\r\n\r\n8:\r\n89919 us\r\n105448 us\r\n98242 us\r\n\r\n9:\r\n89810 us\r\n105629 us\r\n98024 us\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>IR</summary>\r\n\r\n- diff at line 76, from `call-utility` to `call-utility validated`\r\n\r\nbefore:\r\n```\r\nFunction _ready()\r\n 0: line 7:     for i in OUTER_LOOPS:\r\n 2: assign stack(5) = const(10)\r\n 5: for-init (typed INT) stack(3) in stack(5) counter stack(4) end 116\r\n 10: jump 17\r\n 12: for-loop (typed INT) stack(3) in stack(5) counter stack(4) end 116\r\n 17: line 8:            print(\"\\n%s:\" % i)\r\n 19: validated operator stack(12) = const(\"\r\n%s:\") % stack(3)\r\n 24: call-utility stack(13) = print(stack(12))\r\n 30: assign stack(13) = null\r\n 32: line 10:           var start : int\r\n 34: construct validated stack(6) = int()\r\n 39: line 11:           var end : int\r\n 41: construct validated stack(7) = int()\r\n 46: line 13:           start = Time.get_ticks_usec()\r\n 48: call method-bind validated (return) stack(14) = const(object(Time)).get_ticks_usec()\r\n 54: assign stack(6) = stack(14)\r\n 57: line 14:           for j in INNER_LOOPS:\r\n 59: assign stack(10) = const(1000000)\r\n 62: for-init (typed INT) stack(8) in stack(10) counter stack(9) end 87\r\n 67: jump 74\r\n 69: for-loop (typed INT) stack(8) in stack(10) counter stack(9) end 87\r\n 74: line 15:                   var ret : float = sin(j)\r\n 76: call-utility stack(15) = sin(stack(8))\r\n 82: assign stack(11) = stack(15)\r\n 85: jump 69\r\n 87: line 16:           end = Time.get_ticks_usec()\r\n 89: call method-bind validated (return) stack(14) = const(object(Time)).get_ticks_usec()\r\n 95: assign stack(7) = stack(14)\r\n 98: line 17:           print(end - start, \" us\")\r\n 100: validated operator stack(14) = stack(7) - stack(6)\r\n 105: call-utility stack(13) = print(stack(14), const(\" us\"))\r\n 112: assign stack(13) = null\r\n 114: jump 12\r\n 116: == END ==\r\n```\r\n\r\nafter:\r\n```\r\nFunction _ready()\r\n 0: line 7:     for i in OUTER_LOOPS:\r\n 2: assign stack(5) = const(10)\r\n 5: for-init (typed INT) stack(3) in stack(5) counter stack(4) end 116\r\n 10: jump 17\r\n 12: for-loop (typed INT) stack(3) in stack(5) counter stack(4) end 116\r\n 17: line 8:            print(\"\\n%s:\" % i)\r\n 19: validated operator stack(12) = const(\"\r\n%s:\") % stack(3)\r\n 24: call-utility stack(13) = print(stack(12))\r\n 30: assign stack(13) = null\r\n 32: line 10:           var start : int\r\n 34: construct validated stack(6) = int()\r\n 39: line 11:           var end : int\r\n 41: construct validated stack(7) = int()\r\n 46: line 13:           start = Time.get_ticks_usec()\r\n 48: call method-bind validated (return) stack(14) = const(object(Time)).get_ticks_usec()\r\n 54: assign stack(6) = stack(14)\r\n 57: line 14:           for j in INNER_LOOPS:\r\n 59: assign stack(10) = const(1000000)\r\n 62: for-init (typed INT) stack(8) in stack(10) counter stack(9) end 87\r\n 67: jump 74\r\n 69: for-loop (typed INT) stack(8) in stack(10) counter stack(9) end 87\r\n 74: line 15:                   var ret : float = sin(j)\r\n 76: call-utility validated stack(15) = sin(stack(8))\r\n 82: assign stack(11) = stack(15)\r\n 85: jump 69\r\n 87: line 16:           end = Time.get_ticks_usec()\r\n 89: call method-bind validated (return) stack(14) = const(object(Time)).get_ticks_usec()\r\n 95: assign stack(7) = stack(14)\r\n 98: line 17:           print(end - start, \" us\")\r\n 100: validated operator stack(14) = stack(7) - stack(6)\r\n 105: call-utility stack(13) = print(stack(14), const(\" us\"))\r\n 112: assign stack(13) = null\r\n 114: jump 12\r\n 116: == END ==\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-19T08:08:46Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T17:45:40Z","closed_at":"2026-09-23T17:18:55Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"b86cbc415ae83602d855a7870e9632be0effaf4d","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":